ARM L — does verify_auto (a DERIVED project check, run in-loop) convert the small model's complete-but-wrong
task-10 outputs into PASSES, on top of lever N (now default-on)? (review lever L4; Zak-Code #429;
ZAKCODE_VERIFY_AUTO=1)
Pre-registered 2026-09-13 11:16 UTC, BEFORE launch. Branch arm-l-verify-auto. Build: origin/main 0c0bbc4
(lever N default-ON since #439; verify_auto opt-in since #429). Bench src on zc-01 re-synced to 0c0bbc4 and
verified: config default=True (lever N on), derive_verify_command present, tasks.py 657b87bb.

MECHANISM. verify_auto ON => the R1 project-verifier gate derives its command from what the workspace
DECLARES. Task 10's Makefile declares `lint: python -m ruff check .` and `test: python -m pytest`, so
derive_verify_command yields `python -m ruff check . && python -m pytest` (single-line recipes, no make
syntax). The gate requires that command to pass after a code change; the model's own `python -m pytest` does
not match the full derived command, so the harness runs it at the turn's completion point (_try_project_verify,
kind="project_verify", at most attempt_cap=2 harness runs/turn) and injects the real output. A gate that keeps
failing ends the turn stop_reason=verification_failed.

WHY NOW (trigger, previously deferred). Arm K's 12 basins produced 0 lint-class failures, so verify_auto would
not have fired and arm L was DEFERRED. Two 2026-09-13 arms unlocked it: arm J (35B shipped a docstring ruff
violation on task 10, passed 1/3, never ran the project lint in-loop) and arm R (27B shipped a genuine
`make lint` E501 failure, 1/12 --no-pin, PLUS 2 contract failures — parse_duration not-exported and a
ValueError on '0s' — that `pytest` would catch). So the derived `ruff check && pytest` targets THREE observed
failure modes.

INTERACTION WITH LEVER N (the honest framing). Lever N is now DEFAULT-ON, so BOTH cells carry it; arm L
isolates verify_auto's MARGINAL effect on top of lever N. Complementarity hypothesis: lever N gets the small
model to FINISH (doom -> complete), and verify_auto ensures it finishes CORRECTLY (catches the
complete-but-wrong that those completions produce).

MODEL zds-qwen3.6-35b (the primary small-model subject; arm J's trigger; worse-behaved than the 27B, so more
complete-but-wrong for the gate to catch). TASK 10-rule-in-pyproject. temperature 0, stable identity, survey
ON, --no-pin (basin diversity, rb-10849). Runner /root/zb-arml.sh; scorer /root/arml-summary.py; dumps
/root/zb-dumps/L-* (NEVER committed; instruments print counts/hashes only); result JSONs
bench/results/determinism-zakcode-pinOFF-temp0-10-rule-in-pyproject.L-*.json.

CELLS. L-{BASE,AUTO}-35B-10, N=6 per arm, two interleaved blocks of three: BASE b1, AUTO b1, BASE b2, AUTO b2
(basin drift, rb-10849 non-stationarity, hits both arms).
  BASE = shipped default (survey on, lever N on, verify_auto OFF).
  AUTO = shipped default + ZAKCODE_VERIFY_AUTO=1.

MEASURE FIRST (before scoring): per cell — n; pass = count(verify_rc==0); the FAILED runs' verify_out (lint vs
contract, to confirm they are verify_auto-catchable); trace_interventions.project_verify per run; stop reasons
(verification_failed = the gate gave up); turns.

GATE-FIRES CHECK (guard-5501, prove the diagnostic CAN fire): at least one AUTO run must show the gate FIRING —
project_verify >= 2 (a first failing run forced a re-run) OR stop_reason==verification_failed OR a failing
verify exit in the dumps. If the gate never fired under AUTO, L1/L2 are scored "NOT EXERCISED", not a verdict.

RULES.
  L1: AUTO pass rate >= BASE + 2 (of 6) AND the gate fired -> verify_auto buys outcomes on top of lever N ->
      ship verify_auto default-ON (a workspace declaring no check is unaffected — derive returns None, gate inert).
  L2: |AUTO - BASE| <= 1 -> no marginal outcome effect at N=6 -> keep opt-in; report the gate-fire count and
      whether the derived check ever actually failed.
  L3: AUTO <= BASE - 2 -> verify_auto COSTS outcomes (the injected output derails the model) -> keep opt-in,
      name the mechanism from the dumps.
  L4 (descriptive): project_verify runs/run; turns and wall medians; stop reasons.

PREDICTIONS: BASE 3-5/6 (lever N on lifts it above the old doom-dominated rate); AUTO 5-6/6 with 1-2
project_verify runs/run and +1-3 turns; AUTO stops mostly `completed`. Cost ~12 runs x 190-470s = 45-90 min.

VERDICT RULE: L1 (and the gate fired) -> ship verify_auto default-on; L2 or L3 -> keep opt-in with the
measured reason. If NOT EXERCISED (gate never fired), the arm is inconclusive -> re-run on a basin census that
shows a failure, do not score a verdict.
